The **Dirty Pipe** vulnerability (CVE-2022-0847) is a Linux kernel exploit that allows an unprivileged user to overwrite arbitrary files, including sensitive system files like `/etc/passwd`, leading to **privilege escalation**. It was discovered by **Max Kellermann** in 2022 and affects Linux kernels **5.8 and later**.

